# World Cup Market Intelligence v0

Open-source framework for tracking prediction-market dynamics around FIFA World Cup 2026.

This project is not a betting tip service. It is a reusable market-intelligence system for studying how prices, liquidity, narratives and catalysts evolve around a scheduled global event.

## Core idea

The FIFA World Cup 2026 is a fixed-window global attention event: 48 teams, 104 matches, June 11 to July 19, 2026. The system treats it as a live laboratory for prediction-market analysis.

```text
Polymarket / event schedule / news notes
        ↓
market snapshots
        ↓
scoring + narrative classification
        ↓
daily market intelligence brief
        ↓
X / Substack / research archive
```

## What v0 does

- Tracks a curated watchlist of prediction markets
- Pulls public Polymarket market/event data where available
- Stores daily snapshots as CSV/JSON
- Scores markets using a transparent heuristic model
- Classifies signals as structural / tactical / speculative
- Generates a daily Markdown brief
- Keeps the system portable for future events: elections, FOMC, Olympics, crypto launches, AI conferences, token unlocks

## What v0 does not do

- It does not place trades
- It does not provide betting picks
- It does not guarantee edge
- It does not scrape copyrighted match footage
- It does not rely on private APIs

## Quick start

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/world-cup-market-intelligence.git
cd world-cup-market-intelligence
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e .
cp .env.example .env
python scripts/init_watchlist.py
python scripts/update_snapshot.py
python scripts/generate_brief.py
```

Generated output:

```text
data/processed/snapshot_latest.csv
briefs/YYYY-MM-DD-world-cup-market-brief.md
```

## Repository structure

```text
src/wcmi/                 Core package
scripts/                  Runnable scripts
data/raw/                 Raw API outputs / manual inputs
data/processed/           Cleaned snapshots
templates/                Markdown brief templates
docs/                     Architecture and methodology
tests/                    Basic tests
```

